experiment.prespecified:
Fixed 2026-11-20, before any zoo result was read (borg-reborn-rs#713, PR #717). Per RULES 16 the pilot (classes-18,
100,000 turns) runs first with all four arms. Gate:
- no config_error; one binary; each arm's value in borg.txt and in params-core.json of the death replays;
- every cell ends in death, turn_cap or borg_stopped; frozen-turn bursts classified, key outliers listed;
- death bundles reproduced.
Then classes-1800-big (starts 361-900, 60 per class, 100,000 turns) with the same four arms, if the pilot passes.
Report per arm and per class, from every game's messages:
- deaths and causes, final and maximum level, deepest level; paired rescued and newly killed against off;
- deaths with an immobile monster (NEVER_MOVE) adjacent in the last 50 decisions, by monster;
- "# Stepping away from immobile" notes (and "kept at range"), most per game, and any loop (many steps at one monster);
- blows taken from immobile monsters ("The <monster> touches/gazes/releases spores at you"), per game;
- throws and shots at immobile monsters, and immobile monsters killed;
- games where a stair flow passed through a kept creature's reach (blows taken on the way to stairs).
The shipped value (2) is kept, changed or reverted from this result; no claim before it (RULES 14).
